You can buy movies, VOD and on demand.

534
00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:41.620
So exciting.

535
00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.220
And you said it took six years.

536
00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:44.960
So this is like a big moment for you.

537
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:45.520
Yeah.

538
00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:49.840
I mean, it shouldn't have taken six years, but yeah, between the COVID and the strikes and

539
00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.360
the, yeah, the holiday delays of it all, it took a while.

540
00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:53.980
Clark, I really enjoyed this movie.

541
00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:57.340
It stars our office friend, Jake Lacey.

542
00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:57.620
Yeah.

543
00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.740
In a really amazing role, and he's really good in it.

544
00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:06.700
He plays a drunk, barely employed guy.

545
00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.220
Ex-military-ish.

546
00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:08.520
Yep.

547
00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:09.440
Yeah.

548
00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:24.540
I did not know who was going to, quote unquote, win it all.

549
00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:24.880
Yeah.

550
00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:25.160
Good.

551
00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:29.140
But also, Ashley Benson, she plays the female lead.

552
00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:31.360
She plays a stripper.

553
00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:31.660
Yep.

554
00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.120
She's a mom.

555
00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.440
She really needs medicine for her daughter.

556
00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.080
They don't have the money.

557
00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.800
She's a reluctant stripper, though.

558
00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.620
She doesn't really want to be there.

559
00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.260
I mean—

560
00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.640
She has dreams of California.

561
00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:45.640
She has dreams, yeah.

562
00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.740
But nobody, like, you know, makes her work.

563
00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:51.900
I mean, the interesting stuff thematically to me is just, like, when she's watching, seeing

564
00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:56.320
her watch stuff on social media and how she's, like, influenced by, you know, the kind of,

565
00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:00.180
like, more glamorous, like, people she's seeing their Christmas on her phone.

566
00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:00.640
Yeah.

567
00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:05.660
Because that flattening out effect that, like, that the internet has had on—you know, because

568
00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.980
I remember, like, when I was in, like, high school in Arkansas, there was still kind

569
00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:08.880
of, like, regional culture.

570
00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:14.060
And I feel like now with social media, that doesn't really exist anymore.

571
00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.000
I mean, it's really, like, more of a monoculture than ever.

572
00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.040
It's, like, it's weird because there's some—like, it's, like, the Super Bowl is the only thing

573
00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.160
everybody watches still, and everything's very, like, divvied up.

574
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.200
But there's—at the same time, it flattened everything out.

575
00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.980
So, like, it was interesting to me that, you know, these people in these rural places are

576
00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:32.460
still watching the same content as these, like, people in West Hollywood.

577
00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:33.260
Yeah.

578
00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.500
And what does that do to your psyche?

579
00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:35.300
Right.

580
00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.740
And Christmas heightens everything.

581
00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.440
The movie's set at Christmastime and, like—

582
00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:38.700
It is.

583
00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:38.980
Yeah.

584
00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:39.180
Yeah.

585
00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.800
Christmas makes everybody bonkers.

586
00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:41.580
Right.

587
00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.440
Because it's, like, you want to make sure you get everyone the great gifts, and you decorate,

588
00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.520
and you look around, and you're like, oh, our stuff is all crap.

589
00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.560
You're comparing your life to other people's lives more than ever at Christmas.

590
00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:53.440
You know, if you're lonely, it heightens that.

591
00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.720
If you're sad, it heightens that.

592
00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.860
If you're desperate, it heightens that.

593
00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:57.100
It heightens that.

594
00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.460
If you want to rob a strip club, it heightens that.

595
00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.000
Which brings us to—

596
00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.180
I wasn't going to say that part.

597
00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.400
That's not a spoiler.

598
00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:05.360
That's the premise of the movie.

599
00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:05.680
Okay, okay, okay.

600
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:06.280
Yeah.

601
00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.260
Well, why don't you—you'll do a better job of explaining the premise of the movie.

602
00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.020
Give it to us.

603
00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:15.000
I mean, you've basically already done it, but it's about a stripper who, at Christmastime,

604
00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:19.560
down on her luck, tired of her life, decides to rob the strip club she works at

605
00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:23.660
with the help of her former military husband, who is played by The Office's Jake Lacey,

606
00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.400
who really does do just an awesome job of the movie.

607
00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.460
Like, he's so fun.

608
00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:29.140
Your cast is phenomenal.

609
00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.660
You have Justin Long.

610
00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:31.940
That performance was amazing.

611
00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:35.660
When he first came on screen, it took me a minute, and then I realized who it was.

612
00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:36.040
Same.

613
00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:39.340
And then also you have Ron Perlman, which is amazing, and Martin Fisher.

614
00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:40.780
I mean, I could go on and on.

615
00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.120
This cast is really good.

616
00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.400
Yeah, I want to shout out two of the other women in the movie that blew me away,

617
00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:47.600
who are Cody Kennedy and Elle King.

618
00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.920
Just great performances by all the women in this film.

619
00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.380
I was also rooting for the gal with the neck brace.

620
00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.580
She's really who I'm rooting for.

621
00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:56.600
That's Elle King, who—

622
00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:56.820
Yeah.

623
00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.200
Do you guys know—you know, Elle King's a big country music superstar.

624
00:19:59.620 --> 00:19:59.740
Yeah.

625
00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:00.420
Like, do you guys know her?

626
00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:00.900
I don't.

627
00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:01.780
I knew her name.

628
00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:02.420
She's awesome.

629
00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.100
Yeah, but I didn't realize she acted.

630
00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.220
She really hasn't before.

631
00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.660
I just asked her out of the blue.

632
00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:07.680
It just jumped out at me.

633
00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:08.860
It's like, I just had a feeling.

634
00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.460
I was really rooting for her.

635
00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:14.700
We also want to shout out Angela Duke as the pharmacist, because she crushed it.

636
00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:16.340
So that was all improv, by the way.

637
00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.180
No way.

638
00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:17.640
Yeah.

639
00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:18.340
Stop it.

640
00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.740
That was only scripted as one line.

641
00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.580
And my mom goes, can I try something?

642
00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.260
And I go, you can do anything you want.

643
00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.300
Yeah, I'll put two cameras up, and Jake will keep up.

644
00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:25.640
Her on the phone?

645
00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.300
Her on the phone was all improv?

646
00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:27.900
Whole thing.

647
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:28.620
No, that's scripted.

648
00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.060
Wow.

649
00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.300
I just said, do anything you want.

650
00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.360
I'm going to put two cameras up so you can talk over each other, whatever.

651
00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.820
And I was like, Jake will keep up with whatever you do.

652
00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.860
She takes multiple phone calls.

653
00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:38.050
I know.

654
00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:39.280
And puts people on hold.

655
00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:39.700
Yeah.

656
00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:42.180
She must have had a whole vision for her character.

657
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:42.760
She did, yeah.

658
00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:43.900
Is your mom an actress?

659
00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.160
Not professionally.

660
00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.940
But she is SAG eligible now, having been in my two filMs.

661
00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.140
I feel like you have to cast your mom in every movie you make.

662
00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:51.500
Yeah.

663
00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:54.420
The next one, I don't know if there's a part for her, but I agree.

664
00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:55.800
She's also good.

665
00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.200
She's really good.

666
00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:57.420
Yeah.

667
00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:00.140
Before I knew it was your mom, we traded messages.

668
00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:03.160
I was like, I love the pharmacist lady.

669
00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:03.360
That's great.

670
00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.660
And then Gina wrote a note.

671
00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.240
Oh, it says her name's Angela Duke.

672
00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:08.920
I wonder if there are any relation.

673
00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.480
And then I'm like, it's his mom.

674
00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:11.560
Yeah.

675
00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:12.340
Yeah.

676
00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:14.280
And then your brother's in the movie as well.

677
00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:14.440
He is.

678
00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.860
And you co-wrote it with your brother.

679
00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.200
So what's it like working with your family members like that?

680
00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.560
It's nice.

681
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:21.860
You know, it's interesting.

682
00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.780
I mean, the relationship with my brother has been really great and kind of started during

683
00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.180
COVID.

684
00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:29.780
Like right when COVID started, I had just rented these office spaces for us.

685
00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:34.860
So me and him and his friend and writing partner from college, Billington, who wrote the movie

686
00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:39.400
with us, just kind of started getting together every day for like, you know, a year or whatever.

687
00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:41.920
And just like we banged out like multiple scripts.

688
00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.480
So now we kind of had this backlog of scripts, which is great, but it was good.

689
00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:49.940
It was like the intensity of it and just the like the routine of it kind of gave me a work

690
00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:54.380
ethic and like a type of approach to the writing that I had not had before of just kind of

691
00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:56.460
being like workmanlike and joblike about it.

692
00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:59.800
And nobody will be more honest with you or brutal with you than your brother.

693
00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:00.520
Right.

694
00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:02.260
Like if it sucks, he's going to tell you it sucks.

695
00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:04.340
And if it's good, he's going to tell you it's good.

696
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.820
And you can believe it because he just told you you suck.

697
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:07.680
Right, right.

698
00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.900
So yeah, it's been a really great, rewarding, creative partnership we've had.

699
00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:14.960
And yeah, he's going to be in the next one we co-wrote and he's going to be in.

700
00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:16.260
That's so great.

701
00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:21.420
Now we should say you are not in this movie, but you also are.

702
00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:22.860
Your Instagram is in it.

703
00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:26.800
Yeah, that's my cameo in the films is Jake's character DMs me on Instagram.

704
00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.840
Yeah, he's the real life Clark.

705
00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:31.400
DMs the real, yeah, the meta real life Clark Duke.

706
00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:32.940
And he's asking for money.

707
00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:35.300
That was based on a real DM I got.

708
00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:36.760
I was going to ask you about that.

709
00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:38.660
Have you ever received a DM like that?

710
00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:39.200
I have.

711
00:22:39.300 --> 00:22:43.040
I have received that DM, including the angry like follow-up ones.

712
00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:43.720
Really?

713
00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:44.140
Yeah.

714
00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:46.180
This is what I had just got on Instagram.

715
00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:50.060
Like, because I never had Instagram until like, like 2020 when I made the first movie

716
00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:51.820
Arkansas and they asked me Lionsgate.

717
00:22:51.940 --> 00:22:54.160
Because I never had any social media because I just, I don't know.

718
00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:54.980
I just wasn't that interested.

719
00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:56.680
But they asked me to get one.

720
00:22:56.720 --> 00:22:57.080
So I did.

721
00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:00.440
And, you know, you know, you just, you get this inbox full of just like.

722
00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:01.580
A lot, a lot.

723
00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:02.420
Yeah, it's a lot.

724
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:02.880
It's a lot.

725
00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:03.640
You get crazies.

726
00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:04.420
You get all kinds of stuff.

727
00:23:04.680 --> 00:23:06.120
You get, you know, most people are really nice.

728
00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:06.640
Yeah.

729
00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:09.220
But for the most part, I think like that's bad for you too.

730
00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:13.420
So I try to just avoid like all of it because I think the really complimentary stuff is probably

731
00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:14.920
as unhealthy as the really mean stuff.

732
00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:18.080
But yeah, that, that was all, that was based on a real deal.

733
00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:18.480
My God.

734
00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:26.520
I kept thinking that at the very end of the movie that his phone was going to light up

735
00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:28.740
and you would have sent him like a thousand dollars.

736
00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:30.700
And then, and then.

737
00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.660
I waited all the way to the end of the credits, Clark.

738
00:23:32.660 --> 00:23:32.960
I know.

739
00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:36.680
And then, and then after the credits, wait, after the credits, there is a phone.

740
00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:38.880
And I was like, and I said, Jenna, that's it here.

741
00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.460
And then, but it was, he was cheating.

742
00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:41.900
The guy.

743
00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:42.220
Yeah.

744
00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:42.720
Yeah.

745
00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:43.520
Yeah.

746
00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:44.080
Yeah.

747
00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:44.340
Yeah.

748
00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:46.600
That may, yeah, that yours may be better to be honeSt.

749
00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:48.280
I think your pitch may be better.

750
00:23:48.640 --> 00:23:49.520
Oh, well.

751
00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:51.420
There's nothing I can do about it now, but that's a good one.

752
00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:52.320
Call me next time.

753
00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:52.480
Yeah.

754
00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:54.580
We did.

755
00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.380
We were like, it's going to pay off.

756
00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:57.040
It's going to pay off.

757
00:23:57.040 --> 00:23:58.880
And Jenna was like, I don't think so.

758
00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:00.380
And I, and then I was like, no, there's a phone.

759
00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:01.020
There's a phone.

760
00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:02.160
And we're like trading messages.

761
00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:06.360
Well, I feel like, I mean, I feel like we closed that storyline because that's sort

762
00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:11.020
of like the final, you know, that rejection that Tim gets from Clark Duke leaving him

763
00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:11.620
on the red.

764
00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:12.240
Yes.

765
00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:14.420
Sort of what pushes him over the edge.

766
00:24:14.460 --> 00:24:15.020
It does.

767
00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:16.320
That and a lot of alcohol.

768
00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:17.760
He's like, no one cares about us.

769
00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:18.740
Yeah.

770
00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:19.880
Like, I don't feel seen.

771
00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:20.640
Yeah.

772
00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:22.260
Seen, but not seen.

773
00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:24.640
So I feel like it would have been overkill to it.

774
00:24:24.740 --> 00:24:25.920
But no, that would have worked.

775
00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:26.720
That would have worked.

776
00:24:26.720 --> 00:24:29.680
To be fair, it would have been a little bit of a cheap joke.

777
00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:30.460
I'm on the fence.

778
00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:31.720
You're on the fence about it.

779
00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:33.180
I'm 50, 50 years may be better.

780
00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:35.080
Yeah.

781
00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:36.400
You know what?

782
00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:38.800
What would Ralph and Tim say?

783
00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:39.780
They'd say, go back.

784
00:24:39.820 --> 00:24:40.440
Let's reshoot.

785
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:40.840
Yeah.

786
00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:42.980
It's a phone in a field.

787
00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:45.700
Honestly, I shot that, that phone shot in my yard.

788
00:24:46.100 --> 00:24:48.500
We built a fire and wafted it.

789
00:24:48.680 --> 00:24:50.440
And I set a tripod up and filmed that.

790
00:24:50.880 --> 00:24:51.780
Here in LA?

791
00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:52.600
